            <ArticleTitle>Prominent allergist group makes the case for more specialty referrals of asthma cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>28-31, 17</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The American College of Allergy, Asthma, and Immunology maintains that too many managed care organizations are blocking access to specialty clinicians, and as a result asthmatics are not getting appropriate care. In a new report, the group is urging a shift in policies and practice that it maintains will substantially reduce utilization and costs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
